sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant OS as Order Service
    participant CS as Catalog Service
    participant PS as Payment Service
    participant PA as PaymentProvider adapter
    participant K as Kafka
    participant NS as Notification Service

    Note over C,GW: Client already holds a JWT from POST /auth/login

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
    Note over C,NS: Happy path
    C->>GW: POST /orders with items
    GW->>OS: POST /orders, validated JWT
    OS->>CS: Feign POST /internal/inventory/reserve
    CS-->>OS: reservation held, stock moved to reserved
    OS->>OS: persist PENDING + outbox OrderCreated
    OS-->>GW: 201 OrderResponse status PENDING
    GW-->>C: 201 OrderResponse status PENDING
    OS->>K: OrderCreated on orders.v1
    K->>NS: OrderCreated notification

    C->>GW: POST /payments, Idempotency-Key header
    GW->>PS: POST /payments, validated JWT
    PS->>PS: persist PENDING attempt, enforce key uniqueness
    PS->>PA: createPayment with provider idempotency key
    PA-->>PS: providerPaymentId, simulated adapter by default
    PS-->>GW: 201 PaymentResponse status PENDING
    GW-->>C: 201 PaymentResponse status PENDING

    C->>GW: POST /payments/{id}/confirm outcome SUCCEEDED
    GW->>PS: confirm, verify ownership
    PS->>PA: confirmPayment / provider lookup
    PA-->>PS: SUCCEEDED
    PS->>PS: status SUCCESS + audit transition
    PS->>K: PaymentSucceeded on payments.v1
    K->>NS: PaymentSucceeded notification
    K->>OS: PaymentSucceeded on payments.v1, dedupe by eventId
    OS->>CS: Feign POST /internal/inventory/reservations/{orderId}/commit
    CS-->>OS: reservation consumed
    OS->>OS: PENDING -> CONFIRMED
    OS->>K: OrderConfirmed on orders.v1
    K->>NS: OrderConfirmed notification
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
    Note over C,NS: Failed payment path
    C->>GW: POST /payments/{id}/confirm outcome FAILED
    GW->>PS: confirm, verify ownership
    PS->>PA: confirmPayment / provider lookup
    PA-->>PS: FAILED with failure code
    PS->>PS: status FAILED + audit transition
    PS->>K: PaymentFailed on payments.v1
    K->>OS: PaymentFailed on payments.v1, dedupe by eventId
    OS->>CS: Feign POST /internal/inventory/reservations/{orderId}/release
    CS-->>OS: reservation released to available stock
    OS->>OS: PENDING -> FAILED
    OS->>K: OrderFailed on orders.v1
    K->>PS: OrderFailed, flag PENDING attempts for refund if they settle late
    K->>NS: OrderFailed notification
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 230)
    Note over C,NS: Cancellation and late-success compensation - intended behavior
    C->>GW: POST /orders/{id}/cancel while order is PENDING
    GW->>OS: cancel, verify ownership
    OS->>CS: Feign release reservation
    OS->>OS: PENDING -> CANCELLED
    OS->>K: OrderCancelled on orders.v1
    K->>PS: OrderCancelled, mark PENDING attempts cancel-requested
    NS->>NS: OrderCancelled notification from orders.v1

    Note over PA,PS: Provider settles after the order was cancelled
    PA-->>PS: webhook or reconciliation reports SUCCEEDED
    PS->>PS: PENDING -> SUCCESS, cancellation flag detected
    PS->>PA: refund full amount, reason late_success_after_termination
    PA-->>PS: refund SUCCEEDED or PENDING
    alt refund completed immediately
        PS->>PS: status REFUNDED
        PS->>K: RefundCompleted on payments.v1
    else refund pending
        PS->>PS: status REFUND_PENDING
        PS->>K: RefundPending on payments.v1
        Note over PS,K: reconciliation later emits RefundCompleted
    end
    Note over OS,K: Intended: order must not keep a captured payment after cancellation.<br/>Current code refunds at the payment layer; a CANCELLED or FAILED order<br/>is not transitioned to REFUND_PENDING / REFUNDED because order.refund()<br/>only accepts CONFIRMED or REFUND_PENDING. Treat that gap as open.
    end
